bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "Catalog html at device scale 4, interpreter, cpu_simd: giving a lead-space run its exact pen origin (Chrome's quarter device phase; html 4x 0.11 -> 0.10) costs about 3% user CPU: median 19.26 s base vs 19.89 s fix over 4 alternating rounds (seed1126b, base 531e49cc972); animation 15.29 s vs 15.36-15.69 s. RSS flat. A control with the same code forced back onto base's pixels ran at base CPU (18.3 s vs 18.6 s), so the cost follows the changed glyph phases, not the layout code. Likely cause, NOT measured: runs now start on quarter phases no earlier run used, so more (glyph, size, phase) cells are rasterised on first use (phase cell cache in src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/text_layout/font_renderer.spl:501-509). Proposed measurement: a miss counter on the phase-cell cache / atlas, printed per render, compared base vs fix on html 4x; if misses explain the time, share the phase-independent outline work across phases or pre-size the cell cache."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28, P3, open, "web render: Chrome-matching run start phases at k=4 cost ~3% CPU on catalog html (suspected first-use quarter-phase glyph cells)", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/text_layout/font_renderer.spl, 501, "PAGE_DEVICE_SCALE=4 SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter SIMPLE_2D_BACKEND=cpu_simd simple run examples/06_io/ui/web_render_page_ppm.spl examples/06_io/ui/web_catalog/html.html out.ppm 900 760, alternating A/B vs base", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 anim-regress lane: A/B numbers above; pre-#12215 parent d15302e5bf9 html 19.24 s. No document/paint split exists in web_render_page_ppm.spl output. Owner decision on accepting the cost is pending."
    web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 webrender-glyph-raster-cost lane (work/webrender-glyph-raster-cost-20261128, base 2bc96bcf7de, seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b): MEASURED the suspected cause with a temporary print per sfnt_gray_outline_raster call. html / css-paint / animation 4x: calls == distinct (outline, phase) cells (391 / 322 / 239), no memo drops, so the phase-cell cache repeats nothing and each new quarter phase costs one replay. The repeat was 69 / 67 / 52 full re-walks, mostly because a narrow glyph (ir width <= 32, padded area <= 1024, most 64 px lowercase) takes the mask plane of _lcd_aaa_mask, which was never recorded, so every phase after the first re-ran edge build + walk. Fix: the mask-plane walk records too and _gray_aaa_replay replays into either blitter; _gray_aaa_convex_at keeps a phase whose path is convex (f32 rounding: Nunito . at 64 px, I at 60/69 px) on the direct fill. html 4x after (measured on html only): 182 first walks, 190 replays, 19 re-walk calls over 18 unrecorded outlines (6 convex, 6 fat rect, 6 aborted records). Interpreter dispatch totals (SIMPLE_INTERP_PROFILE=1) base -> fix at k=4: overview 73349838 -> 73041092 (-0.42%), html 858973022 -> 857652016 (-0.15%), css-layout 1091337057 -> 1090360240 (-0.09%), css-paint 1597943824 -> 1596693788 (-0.08%), forms-media 323440446 -> 322264541 (-0.36%), animation 285311373 -> 284385275 (-0.32%), evidence 44298761 -> 43477216 (-1.85%), tab-bar 23599487 -> 23190693 (-1.73%); k=1: html +0.01%, forms-media +0.04%, css-layout -0.03%, the rest within noise (same-code repeats differ by ~2k; the 1x pages hold a few large gray glyphs and the per-replay convex test costs slightly more there than it saves). All 16 PPM sha1 byte-identical to base. html 4x, 3 alternated rounds: user CPU median 91.25 s -> 89.16 s and max RSS median 3281668 -> 3283640 KB (+2 MB records): no regression, within noise. The gain is small (about 0.15% of the ~3% in the description on html) and the suspected cache-miss cause measured false: the residual is first-use cells at replay cost (~80k dispatches each, nearly all row writes), see web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28."
    web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28, 2, "2026-11-28 re-scoped, back to open (review of work/webrender-glyph-raster-cost-20261128): FIXED here: the narrow-glyph full re-walks (mask-plane walks are now recorded and replayed; convex-at-phase and head-sentinel guards keep replays exact), about 0.15% of the ~3% on html 4x. The suspected cause (phase-cell cache misses) measured false: calls == distinct cells. REMAINS: each first-use quarter-phase cell costs one replay (~80k interpreter dispatches, nearly all trapezoid row writes + flush), so Chrome-matching run phases still add roughly the measured ~3% user CPU on html 4x. Fix candidates: the seed-kernel / JIT options of web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28 (a kernel for the replay row writer), or measure on the JIT lane."

